Within the $U_1$ leptoquark model, precision data from $b 	o c$ transitions offer significant constraints, yet currently available experiments lack sufficient sensitivity to adequately limit certain decay processes, such as $\Lambda_b 	o p 	au  ar{
u}$. A detailed analysis has been conducted to evaluate the effects of $b 	o c$ data on $\Lambda_b 	o p 	au  ar{
u}$ decay processes involving $U_1$ leptoquarks, revealing that while $b 	o c$ data significantly restrict the parameter space of $U_1$, there remain allowable values that align with $\Lambda_b 	o p 	au  ar{
u}$ data, and predicted ratios of branching fractions and polarisation asymmetries are in agreement with experimental values.
